The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (cdclk > 312000)
```
Reason:
This condition does not account for the new cdclk values (324/326.4), leading to incorrect voltage level assignments for cdclk values above 312000 but below 326400, which can affect system performance and stability.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (cdclk > 326400)
	return 3;
else if (cdclk > 312000)
	return 2;
```
Reason:
These updated conditions correctly incorporate the new cdclk values, ensuring that voltage levels are assigned accurately for the specified ranges, thus improving system performance and stability.

